{{!< default}}

{{!-- Every error but a missing URL. Ghost resolves error-404.hbs first and falls back here for
every other status code, so this is a 500, a 503, a rate limit — the cases where the platform's
own message is the only thing on the page that carries information.

That is the one place this Surface departs from error/a1.hbs, whose sentence is the theme's. Here
the heading is `{{message}}` and the list below it is `{{errorDetails}}`, because a reader looking
at a 500 needs Ghost's words, not the theme's.

No subscribe block either. The designed 404 offers the newsletter because a reader who mistyped a
URL is still a reader; someone who has hit a server error is being asked to wait, and a signup
form under a 500 reads as the publication changing the subject.

`{{{this.message}}}` is triple-braced on purpose: Ghost's error details arrive pre-escaped and
double-brace would print the entities. The values come from Ghost, never from a request. --}}

{{> "chrome/header" compact=true}}

<main
	id="main"
	class="flex grow items-center"
	data-surface="error">

	<section
		aria-labelledby="error-h"
		class="container w-full py-26 text-center">
		<p
			aria-hidden="true"
			class="font-display text-ghost-num text-[clamp(88px,16vw,208px)] leading-[0.86] font-medium tracking-[-0.04em]">{{statusCode}}</p>

		<h1
			id="error-h"
			class="font-display tracking-display mx-auto mt-7 max-w-[22ch] text-[clamp(30px,3.6vw,46px)] leading-[1.1] font-medium text-balance">{{message}}</h1>

		<a
			href="{{@site.url}}"
			class="font-ui text-accent mt-8 inline-block text-[14px]">{{t "Back to the front page"}} &rarr;</a>

		{{#if errorDetails}}
			<ul class="font-mono text-muted measure mx-auto mt-10 text-left text-[12px]">
				{{#foreach errorDetails}}
					<li>{{{this.message}}}</li>
				{{/foreach}}
			</ul>
		{{/if}}
	</section>

</main>

{{> "chrome/footer" slim=true}}
